BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Tech Lancaster
UID:event_313614676@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260619T051016Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260625T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260625T203000
SUMMARY:Tech Lancaster Meetup
DESCRIPTION:Tech Lancaster Meetups\nWe will be upstairs in "The Sanctuary"
  - when you walk in the main entrance just head up the stairs! We will hav
 e signs as you walk in to guide you.\nPizza is provided free upstairs. Bee
 r/wine/soda/etc at the bar downstairs!\n\nThis months speakers:\n**Jonatha
 n Bowe - *Out with the Old\, in with the Nu***\nIf you're a fan of automat
 ion and scripting\, you've likely written some Bash or Powershell. There's
  a nu kid on the block that learns from those classic languages and tries 
 to provide a better alternative. We'll look at some of the features of Nus
 hell\, like types and structured data\, some built in tools in the languag
 e\, and rewriting a Bash script in Nushell. Get ready to learn something n
 u!\n\n**Grant Celley** - ***Programmatically making 3d meshes with trimesh
 ***\nIn this talk\, we will explore how to create and manipulate 3D geomet
 ry programmatically using Python\, focusing on the powerful combination of
  NumPy and Trimesh. Rather than relying on traditional modeling tools\, we
 'll generate custom meshes from mathematical definitions\, construct compl
 ex shapes through code\, and learn techniques for modeling. It will cover 
 how Python can be used to create everything from simple primitives to enti
 rely custom 3D assets.\n\nTypical schedule of events:\n\n6:30 PM Doors Ope
 n/Pizza/Mingle\n7:00 PM Introduction/Announcements\n7:05 PM First Speaker\
 n7:35 PM Break\n7:45 PM Speaker 2\n8:15 PM End
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/tech-lancaster-meetups/events/3136146
 76/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260303T075545Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260303T075545Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
